Section 119 (manuscript p.595) studies the homomorphism from an arithmetic fundamental group 𝓜 into a profinite group M_{ρ,σ}(Ẑ)^ attached to the tower of Fermat curves. This group is built from the automorphism groups of the Fermat curves x^N+y^N=1, which are Galois covers of P^1−{0,1,∞} with group (Z/N)^2, together with extra symmetries.

On the previous pages Grothendieck works with group schemes over Z indexed by the level N: Z_{ρ,σ}, G_{ρ,σ}, G^{⇆}_{ρ,σ}, N_ρ, N_σ, M_{ρ,σ}, M^{⇆}_{ρ,σ}. Here he passes to the limit over N ∈ N*. The superscript Δ means 'take the systems of sections compatible along the tower'.

The basic example is O_N (essentially Z/N, or the cyclotomic ring of level N). Its compatible Ẑ-points give Ẑ, and its units give Ẑ*. Using the semidirect product decompositions (150), he obtains the list (216):
- Z_{ρ,σ} ≃ Ẑ*·L̂_0, with L̂_0 = Ẑ·λ_0 ≃ Ẑ;
- G_{ρ,σ} ≃ Ẑ*·𝔖^{+∧};
- G^{⇆}_{ρ,σ} ≃ Ẑ*·M^∧;
- N_ρ ≃ O_{12}^*(Ẑ) ≃ Ẑ*;
- N_σ ≃ Ẑ*·Ẑ, the affine group of Ẑ;
- M̃_{ρ,σ} ≃ Ẑ*·(Ẑ × 𝔖^{+∧});
- M̃^{⇆}_{ρ,σ} ≃ Ẑ*·(Ẑ × M̂).
In each case Ẑ* acts on the right-hand factor through the cyclotomic-type actions computed earlier.

He remarks that, after suitable adjustments of notation, these profinite groups could have been constructed directly from the pair (𝔖^{+∧}, 𝔖^{⇆∧} = M^∧) of §49 VI. Once ρ, σ, τ are chosen, this gives canonical homomorphisms (217): 𝓜 = 𝒩_{1,1}^{ét} → M̃_{ρ,σ}, restricting to M^! → M̃^{⇆}_{ρ,σ}. Here 𝓜 is the étale fundamental group of a moduli-type object of type (1,1) over Q, and M^! is a subgroup of it.

As usual these maps decompose into three components; the next page spells this out:
- The component to N_ρ ≃ Ẑ* is just the cyclotomic character (the 'condition cyclotomique') and raises no interesting question.
- The components to G_{ρ,σ} and G^{⇆}_{ρ,σ}, and to N_σ ≃ Ẑ*⋉Ẑ, raise surjectivity questions. He would hope to attack these 'by the arithmetic route', presuming that π_1(Q) itself surjects.

The problem served is to measure the image of the arithmetic fundamental group, and so of Galois via the Teichmüller tower, in the profinite symmetry groups of the Fermat tower. This is a non-abelian refinement of the cyclotomic character.
